{
 "title": "Figma (design-to-code)",
 "content": "## Overview\n\nEmergent can convert your Figma designs directly into working code. Share a Figma URL in chat and the platform will analyze the design, extract components, styles, and layout structure, then generate production-ready React code that matches your mockup.\n\nThis guide walks you through importing a Figma design and refining the generated implementation.\n\n<Note>\nFigma-to-code works for both web and mobile designs. The platform auto-detects the design type (viewport, frame names, component structure) and generates the appropriate stack.\n</Note>\n\n## Before you start\n\n- **Figma file permissions**: Your design must be shared with \"Anyone with the link can view\" or public. Private files will return a permissions error.\n- **Frame structure**: Organize your design into clearly named frames (e.g. `Homepage`, `Dashboard`, `Mobile - Login`). Emergent treats each top-level frame as a candidate page or screen.\n- **Design system**: If your design uses Figma components, variants, and auto-layout, the generated code will reflect that structure with reusable React components.\n\n## How to convert a Figma design\n\n<Steps>\n<Step title=\"Share your Figma file\">\nIn Figma, click **Share** \u2192 **Copy link**. Ensure the file is publicly viewable or set to \"Anyone with the link.\"\n</Step>\n\n<Step title=\"Paste the URL in chat\">\nIn your Emergent workspace chat, paste the Figma URL and describe what you want:\n\n```\nhttps://www.figma.com/file/abc123/My-Design\nBuild the homepage from this design\n```\n\nYou can reference specific frames by name:\n\n```\nhttps://www.figma.com/file/abc123/Mobile-App\nImplement the \"Onboarding Flow\" screens\n```\n</Step>\n\n<Step title=\"AI analyzes and generates code\">\nEmergent will:\n- Parse the Figma file structure (frames, layers, text, styles)\n- Extract colors, typography, spacing values\n- Identify interactive elements (buttons, inputs, nav)\n- Generate React components with Tailwind CSS (web) or React Native (mobile)\n- Create placeholder logic for any buttons or forms\n\nThis typically takes 30\u201390 seconds depending on design complexity.\n</Step>\n\n<Step title=\"Review the preview\">\nThe generated app opens in the preview pane. Compare it side-by-side with your Figma design to catch layout differences, missing elements, or styling mismatches.\n</Step>\n\n<Step title=\"Iterate in chat\">\nDescribe any changes:\n\n```\nThe hero image should be full-width\nMove the CTA button to the right\nUse the exact blue from the design: #3B82F6\n```\n\nEmergent will adjust the code and refresh the preview. You can iterate as many times as needed.\n</Step>\n</Steps>\n\n## What gets converted\n\n| Design element | How it's handled |\n|----------------|------------------|\n| **Frames** | Top-level frames \u2192 pages or screens; nested frames \u2192 layout sections |\n| **Text layers** | `<h1>`, `<p>`, `<span>` with font family, size, weight, color preserved |\n| **Images** | `<img>` tags with placeholder `src` (you can swap in real assets later) |\n| **Buttons** | `<button>` elements with hover states inferred from Figma variants |\n| **Auto-layout** | Flexbox (`flex`, `justify-between`, `gap-4`) or CSS Grid |\n| **Components** | Reusable React components (e.g. `Button.jsx`, `Card.jsx`) |\n| **Colors & styles** | Tailwind utility classes or CSS variables extracted from fill/stroke |\n| **Icons** | SVG inline or Lucide icon imports (if the icon matches a known name) |\n\n<Warning title=\"Unsupported features\">\n- **Advanced plugins/effects**: Figma plugin data, complex blend modes, and non-standard effects may be simplified or omitted.\n- **Vector editing**: Complex vector shapes are exported as static SVG; you cannot edit paths post-import.\n- **Animations**: Figma Smart Animate and transitions are not carried over. Describe animations in chat after import.\n</Warning>\n\n## Refining the output\n\n### Design inconsistencies\n\nIf the generated layout doesn't match pixel-for-pixel, see the [Design inconsistencies](/design-inconsistencies) troubleshooting guide for common causes (e.g. absolute positioning, overlapping layers, hidden elements).\n\n### Swapping placeholder images\n\nThe import uses placeholder `src` attributes. Replace them in chat:\n\n```\nReplace the hero image with /assets/hero.jpg\n```\n\nOr drop real images into the workspace file tree and update the paths.\n\n### Connecting to a database\n\nFigma designs often show lists, cards, or tables with sample data. After import, wire these to a real backend:\n\n```\nConnect the product cards to MongoDB\nLoad the user list from the database\n```\n\nSee [Database (MongoDB)](/database-mongodb) for setup instructions.\n\n### Adding interactivity\n\nButtons and forms are rendered but not wired. Describe the behavior:\n\n```\nWhen the user clicks \"Sign Up\", show a modal with email and password fields\nOn submit, create a new user in the database\n```\n\nEmergent will generate the event handlers, state management, and API calls.\n\n## Tips for best results\n\n<Tip>\n**Name your layers clearly**. Figma layer names like `Button - Primary`, `Header Logo`, `CTA Section` help the AI understand intent and generate semantic component names.\n</Tip>\n\n<Tip>\n**Use Figma components and variants**. If you have a `Button` component with `Primary` and `Secondary` variants, Emergent will create a single `<Button variant=\"primary\">` React component rather than duplicating code.\n</Tip>\n\n<Tip>\n**Organize with auto-layout**. Designs using Figma's auto-layout (flexbox-style stacking) convert more accurately than absolute-positioned layers.\n</Tip>\n\n<Info>\nIf you're importing a multi-page design, mention which frames to prioritize. For example: \"Start with the Homepage frame, we'll add Dashboard later.\"\n</Info>\n\n## Web \u2194 Mobile conversion\n\nIf you import a web design but later want a mobile version (or vice versa), describe the request in chat:\n\n```\nConvert this to a React Native mobile app\n```\n\nEmergent will adapt the layout, swap web components for native equivalents, and adjust touch targets and navigation. See [Web <-> Mobile conversion](/web-mobile-conversion-canonical) for details.\n\n## Example workflows\n\n<AccordionGroup>\n<Accordion title=\"Landing page from Figma\">\n1. Designer shares a Figma file with `Hero`, `Features`, `Pricing`, `Footer` frames.\n2. Paste URL in chat: \"Build the landing page from this Figma.\"\n3. Emergent generates a Next.js app with four sections, Tailwind styling.\n4. Iterate: \"Make the pricing cards stack on mobile,\" \"Add a contact form in the footer.\"\n5. Deploy to a custom domain.\n</Accordion>\n\n<Accordion title=\"Mobile onboarding flow\">\n1. Figma file has three frames: `Welcome`, `Sign Up`, `Permissions`.\n2. Paste URL: \"Create the onboarding screens from this design.\"\n3. Emergent builds a React Native app with navigation between screens.\n4. Add logic: \"Store the user's name in MongoDB after they complete sign-up.\"\n5. Test on the mobile preview.\n</Accordion>\n\n<Accordion title=\"Dashboard with live data\">\n1. Figma dashboard shows charts, KPI cards, and a data table (all static).\n2. Import: \"Build this dashboard.\"\n3. Emergent creates the layout and placeholder data.\n4. Wire to backend: \"Fetch sales data from MongoDB and populate the chart.\"\n5. Add filters: \"Let the user filter by date range.\"\n</Accordion>\n</AccordionGroup>\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n| Issue | Solution |\n|-------|----------|\n| **\"Unable to access Figma file\"** | Check sharing settings. File must be publicly viewable or shared via link. |\n| **Layout doesn't match design** | Simplify overlapping layers, avoid absolute positioning. See [Design inconsistencies](/design-inconsistencies). |\n| **Missing fonts** | Emergent uses web-safe fallbacks. Specify a Google Font or upload a custom font in chat. |\n| **Icons not rendering** | If Figma icons aren't recognized, describe them: \"Replace the placeholder with a lucide `menu` icon.\" |\n| **Colors slightly off** | Copy the exact hex from Figma and paste in chat: \"Change the primary button to #3B82F6.\" |\n\n<Callout type=\"info\" title=\"Need help?\">\nIf the import isn't working as expected, share the Figma URL and a screenshot of the issue in chat. The AI can debug layer structure and adjust the conversion logic.\n</Callout>\n\n## Next steps\n\n<CardGroup cols={2}>\n<Card title=\"Design inconsistencies\" icon=\"triangle-alert\" href=\"/design-inconsistencies\">\nTroubleshoot common Figma-to-code layout mismatches\n</Card>\n<Card title=\"Custom domain\" icon=\"globe\" href=\"/custom-domain\">\nDeploy your design to a production domain\n</Card>\n<Card title=\"Database (MongoDB)\" icon=\"database\" href=\"/database-mongodb\">\nConnect your UI to a real backend\n</Card>\n<Card title=\"Glossary\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"/glossary-of-emergent-terms\">\nLearn platform-specific terms and concepts\n</Card>\n</CardGroup>",
 "description": "Convert Figma designs to code."
}